    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d443">

                <pb facs="0662" n="574" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg574"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hirsch to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-05-19"><hi rendition="#italic">May 19, 1892</hi></date>.
                        (Received June 2.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 451.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am in receipt to-day of the following
                    telegram from the Stamford Manufacturing Company at Alexandretta: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">May</hi> 19, 1892.</p>
                        <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#italic">American Legation,
                                Constinople:</hi></p>
                        <p>To-day regular permit was given. Sincere thanks.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stamford.</hi></p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>I have as yet received but one letter from the company in addition to the
                    telegraphic information which I communicated to the Department in my Nos. 441
                    and 443, but suppose further detailed information will arrive by mail, when
                    copies will be promptly forwarded to the Department.</p>
                <p>The company is now enabled to proceed with their building operations without
                    further hindrance.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Solomon Hirsch.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
